   "evidence": "`code/TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/Pullback.lean:89` `namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` (no `TauCeti`), containing the direct analogues `pullbackOplaxMonoidal` (288), `isMonoidal_pullbackPushforwardAdjunction` (293), `isLocallyFree_pullback` (512), `restrictPullbackObjIso (V : Y.Opens) (M : Y.Modules)` (356), `overEquivFunctorObjFreeIso (U : X.Opens)` (399). Mathlib agrees: `mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/Sheaf.lean:595` `def overFunctorEquiv {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens) : ... \u2245 restrictFunctor U.\u03b9` is in `Scheme.Modules`, not `Scheme.Opens`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/Restriction/Monoidal.lean",
   "fix": "Move these six into `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` (as `TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/Pullback.lean` does, with no `TauCeti` wrapper), update the qualified references and the `## Main declarations` list at lines 26-29, and leave the two quasicoherent theorems where they are.",
   "issue": "`restrictFunctorMonoidal` (50), `pullbackInclusionExactPairing` (59), `pullbackInclusionExactPairing_evaluation` (70), `_coevaluation` (88), `nonempty_hasLeftDual_pullback_inclusion` (104), `nonempty_hasRightDual_pullback_inclusion` (112) are declared in bare `TauCeti`, but they are statements about `Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor`/`Scheme.Modules.pullback`, whose entire TauCeti-side API lives in `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`. A consumer holding `(Scheme.Modules.pullback U.\u03b9).obj M` will not find `TauCeti.nonempty_hasLeftDual_pullback_inclusion`, and the same file already files its quasicoherent analogues under `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentSheaf`, so the file is internally inconsistent too.",
   "line": "50"
  }
 ],
